    "result_text": "Done. The build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `AUDIT` logger** \u2014 `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`, matching the exact logger name the test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches to.\n\n2. **Emitted the audit line on successful create** \u2014 right after `saveOwner(owner)` in `addOwner(...)`, so it only fires once the owner is persisted (and thus has an id, customerCode, and registrationDate assigned):\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe message includes all three required fields. The `registrationDate` is a `LocalDate` whose `toString()` yields ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 identical to how the `date`-formatted DTO field serializes in the JSON the test reads back \u2014 so `audit.anyContains(id, customerCode, registrationDate)` matches. The acceptance test passes and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
